h_load"},{"a":52535,"t":"code","b":[76,240,2],"m":"jmp","oa":752,"o":"api_print_long"},{"a":52538,"l":"shop_member","c":"The party position (1-7) of the member who is trading: 1 by default ($CA60), else the member picked at 'Who wants to enter?' ($CA75). Read for the roster highlight ($CAA1) and by the 'P' key, which pools every other member's cash on this one ($CB5A, $CC40).","t":"byte","b":[0],"x":[51808,51829,51873,52058,52288]},{"a":52539,"l":"item_table_changed","c":"1 after a sale ($CB3B) or a purchase ($CC1D), cleared each time round the shop's loop ($CA53): when set, leaving the sell or the buy list writes the item table at $3100 back to its file (JMP $03C2 at $CB56 and $CC3D), so the stock the shop keeps in byte 2 of each record lasts. A purchase that sells out the last item in stock is the exception: the buy list is then left through message 1 ($CBD3, $CBBA) without the test, the table is not written, and the next time round the loop clears the flag.","t":"byte","b":[0],"x":[51795,52027,52049,52253,52280]},{"a":52540,"l":"party_changed","c":"0 on entry ($CA25), 1 after any sale ($CB3E) or purchase ($CC20): when set, leaving the shop from 'Who wants to enter?' saves the game ($CA85-$CA8A, $02D8). Left-arrow at 'B)uy or S)ell?' in a party of one jumps past that test ($CA98 to $CA8D), so that way out never saves.","t":"byte","b":[0],"x":[51749,51845,52030,52256]},{"a":52541,"l":"shop_text","c":"The shop's packed text block (the engine's format; shop_print_wrapped points $43/$44 here). These 60 bytes are its alphabet: entries $00-$23 are ' ', t, o, n, y, e, a, newline, the end code ($00, code $08), u, r, h, s, l, i, w, m, c, $, {06}, '.', ')', v, p, g, f, d, b, '?', ''', '!', {04}, {03}, k, '=', {0B}; codes $00-$1D give entries $00-$1D, the escape code $1F followed by 0-5 gives entries $1E-$23, and code $1E is the capital shift; $24-$3B are unused $7F.","t":"byte","b":[32,116,111,110,121,101,97,13]},{"a":52549,"t":"byte","b":[0,117,114,104,115,108,105,119]},{"a":52557,"t":"byte","b":[109,99,36,6,46,41,118,112]},{"a":52565,"t":"byte","b":[103,102,100,98,63,39,33,4]},{"a":52573,"t":"byte","b":[3,107,61,11,127,127,127,127]},{"a":52581,"t":"byte","b":[127,127,127,127,127,127,127,127]},{"a":52589,"t":"byte","b":[127,127,127,127,127,127,127,127]},{"a":52597,"t":"byte","b":[127,127,127,127]},{"a":52601,"l":"shop_text_groups","c":"The shop text's group table, three words, each an offset from $CD79 to a group of four messages: +$06 = $CD7F (messages 0-3), +$3E = $CDB7 (4-7), +$8A = $CE03 (8-11).","t":"word","b":[6,0,62,0,138,0],"d":[6,62,138]},{"a":52607,"l":"shop_text_msgs_0_3","c":"Shop messages 0-3, one bit stream: 0 empty (never printed); 1 '{04}We are temporarily out of stock.\\n{06}' (nothing to buy, $CBD3); 2 'Who wants to enter?\\n' ($CA69); 3 '\\n{0B} can't buy anything.\\n{06}' (the member is not conscious, $CA7D). {04} clears the window, {06} waits at '(RETURN)', {0B} is the member's name. Message 3 ends with byte $CDB5; the next byte, $CDB6 ($01), lies before group 1 and is not read.","t":"byte","b":[232,7,255,10,48,170,128,80]},{"a":52615,"t":"byte","b":[224,21,202,40,215,8,16,41]},{"a":52623,"t":"byte","b":[0,145,1,11,34,254,65,207]},{"a":52631,"t":"byte","b":[68,254,45,1,158,25,129,129]},{"a":52639,"t":"byte","b":[32,64,25,161,40,126,208,249]},{"a":52647,"t":"byte","b":[5,68,51,122,0,59,17,96]},{"a":52655,"t":"byte","b":[6,9,203,13,76,207,68,1]},{"a":52663,"l":"shop_text_msgs_4_7","c":"Shop messages 4-7: 4 'P)ool Money = ${03}' (show_pool_line); 5 '\\nYou don't have anything they want!\\n{06}' (nothing to sell, $CAD6); 6 '\\nDo you want to B)uy or S)ell?\\n' ($CAA7); 7 '{04}\\n    $$$      ITEM', the list header ($CACE, $CBBB).","t":"byte","b":[254,86,33,26,240,80,140,66]},{"a":52671,"t":"byte","b":[192,39,64,126,129,142,39,34]},{"a":52679,"t":"byte","b":[1,45,70,15,96,25,91,128]},{"a":52687,"t":"byte","b":[25,36,44,55,48,8,171,16]},{"a":52695,"t":"byte","b":[240,204,8,31,156,137,142,215]},{"a":52703,"t":"byte","b":[2,16,145,192,51,35,128,32]},{"a":52711,"t":"byte","b":[128,223,53,17,32,20,240,172]},{"a":52719,"t":"byte","b":[150,214,248,65,63,28,0,0]},{"a":52727,"t":"byte","b":[144,82,2,0,0,0,222,249]},{"a":52735,"t":"byte","b":[224,139,135,8]},{"a":52739,"l":"shop_text_msgs_8_9","c":"Shop messages 8 and 9, the last the shop prints: 8 'Your inventory is full.\\n{06}' ($CBB5, $CC33); 9 'That costs too much!{03}' ($CC4D). Message 9's end code is in $CE23; the group's messages 10 and 11 would decode from the bytes after it ('mo', '  t'), and nothing asks for them.","t":"byte","b":[158,136,164,128,27,182,140,32]},{"a":52747,"t":"byte","b":[20,1,142,129,156,90,163,103]},{"a":52755,"t":"byte","b":[34,31,150,9,32,10,22,24]},{"a":52763,"t":"byte","b":[8,66,0,152,226,250,224,11]},{"a":52771,"t":"byte","b":[4]},{"a":52772,"l":"shop_last_byte","c":"The last byte module 1's own packed data decodes to ($05): the module is $CA00-$CE24, 1,061 bytes, the same on sides 1, 2 and 4. It follows message 9's end code ($CE23) and nothing reads it: the shop prints messages 1-9 only, and no instruction or pointer in the module reaches past $CE23.","t":"byte","b":[5]},{"a":52773,"t":"gap","n":12763},{"a":52773,"t":"note","l":"shop_tail","c":"$CE25-$CE78: not module 1. The unpacker decodes a 4-page read window ($CE), not the stream's length, and on side 1 (this snapshot) module 3's stream begins 947 bytes into module 1's, so $CE25-$CE60 are module 3's packed bytes decoded with module 1's table, and $CE61-$CE78, 24 zeros, come from the zero bytes after module 3's stream (T25/L8 bytes $7D-$98), where the window ends. Nothing reads them.","note":"outside the tracked image"}]}